            <ArticleTitle>The refractory painful arc syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>544-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Twenty-three patients with a severe refractory painful arc syndrome have been treated by excision of the outer end of the clavicle and division of the coracoacromial ligament through a deltoid-splitting approach. After a follow-up of more than six months all patients have been relieved of night pain. Six still have slight pain on movement, but the rest are symptom-free.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
